From 28c613119bb57fc16b9b528a8ed56037e75dc57e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florent Kermarrec <florent@enjoy-digital.fr>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 10:46:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/22] test: extend AXIBurst2Beat coverage and add focused
 AXI2AXILite test

test_burst2beat:
  - Each burst now carries an explicit `id` and the checker verifies
    that the beat side reports the same id for every beat of that
    burst.  Catches AXIBurst2Beat regressions where id is dropped or
    only forwarded on the first/last beat.
  - The checker also verifies the beat-side `last` signal asserts
    *only* on the final beat of each burst.  Catches off-by-one /
    early-termination bugs the previous address-only check would
    silently miss.
  - Edge cases added: a 1-beat (degenerate) INCR burst and a
    256-beat (max AXI4 burst length) INCR burst.  Together these
    bracket the full burst-length range.

test_axi2axilite_bridge (new):
  Focused test for AXI2AXILite.  We instantiate the bridge alone
  with an AXILiteSRAM behind it (already covered by the AXI-Lite
  tests), and add @passive observers on the AXI-Lite ar / aw
  channels that record per-beat addresses produced by the bridge.

  For each scenario we:
    1. drive a write burst on the AXI master side,
    2. snapshot the captured AXI-Lite aw addresses,
    3. drive the matching read burst,
    4. snapshot the captured AXI-Lite ar addresses,
    5. verify both address sequences match the expected unwrapped
       addresses for that burst type, and the read data matches the
       data we wrote (with FIXED bursts modelled as overwrite-same-
       cell-N-times so all beats read back beats[-1]).

  Scenarios cover INCR-{1,4,16}, FIXED-{4,8} and WRAP-{4,8} mid-block
  starts.  This is the first focused test of the AXI2AXILite bridge
  on bursts; previously it was only exercised indirectly via
  test_axilite2axi2mem (single-beat AXI-Lite reads/writes).

All 18 test_axi.py tests pass; full test_axi.py / test_axi_lite.py
/ test_wishbone.py suites green (69/69 + 25 subtests).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
